  "query_preview": "/Monday through Friday/...\nHigh pressure aloft will rebuild starting Monday as the upper \nlow exits through Montana into southern Canada. The higher \npressure will bring warmer air back into our CWA the rest of \nthe week, with temps rising back to normal or several degrees \nabove Wednesday and beyond. The next upper low is forecast to \nstay off the Oregon coast, but latest models (GFS more than \nECMWF) show southwesterly flow aloft tapping into moisture from \nthe next westward-moving hurricane in the Pacific subtropics. \nWe therefore have a slight chance of thunderstorms in the \nforecast as early as Wednesday afternoon, but more likely\nThursday and Friday.",
